    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3dd768f0-db78-5b00-ad8d-3d14711642cc",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find the value of ${x}_{4}-{x}_{2}$ given that  $6a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-26 \\\\ 48 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-6a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-6a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}-26 \\\\ 48 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}-6\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-14 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{4}-{x}_{2}=-2-(-9)=7.$",
